result:
I've reviewed all available source, tests, the goal config, and the implementation report. The two patch files referenced under `reports/review-bundle/` don't exist in this tree (only the markdown reports are present), so my verdict rests on the actual source and tests, which is the authoritative material.

I walked each of the seven flagged risks against the code and the bounded production command (`--max-cycles 1 --decompose-mode live --apply-mode live_diff --allow-live --live-model … --test-command … --allow-promotion --no-dry-run`).

```json
{
  "verdict": "ACCEPT",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "issue": "Markdown auto-repair runs AFTER the patch gate (validate_unified_diff) and the repaired content is not re-validated through the patch gate's caps/boundary check.",
      "evidence": "diff_proposer.py:163-185 validates response.diff_text, applies it, then _validate_changed_markdown/_repair_markdown_references mutate the file (line 359-385) before recording diff_to_record=_current_diff(...). The patch gate is not re-run on the repaired content.",
      "recommended_fix": "Structurally safe today because _repair_markdown_references only does in-place substring substitution on the single already-validated .md file (cannot add lines/files, links re-checked, loop promotion re-checks staged file-set + boundary). Optionally re-run validate_unified_diff on _current_diff after repair for defense-in-depth."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "issue": "Recorded-patch fidelity has a fallback that could record the pre-repair diff if _current_diff returns empty.",
      "evidence": "diff_proposer.py:172 `diff_to_record = (_current_diff(...) if repaired_markdown else \"\") or response.diff_text`. If a repair nets to no on-disk change, _current_diff is empty and the un-repaired response.diff_text is recorded.",
      "recommended_fix": "Edge case only (a candidate with no net change would fail its gate anyway). Patch is provenance-only — promotion stages actual on-disk content via `git add -- target` (repo_goal_loop.py:650), not the recorded patch — so verified==promoted content regardless. Could assert non-empty current diff when repaired_markdown is True."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "issue": "For a docs/markdown candidate the configured --test-command behaviour gate is not applied; docs promote on their domain (link) gate alone.",
      "evidence": "repo_goal_loop.py:428-440: is_code only for .py or needs_code_change; AGENTS.md (safe_to_patch_docs_only) -> behaviour_gate='not_applicable', promotable=gate_ok. The dry-run's selected candidate was exactly agent.agents-md.missing -> AGENTS.md.",
      "recommended_fix": "This is the documented, intended posture (low-risk docs). Acceptable for one bounded cycle; just be aware --test-command may be unused if the live decomposition selects a docs candidate."
    }
  ],
  "report_overclaims": [],
  "summary": "Safe enough for the bounded one-cycle production-live fmc-mcp command. All seven flagged risks are closed and test-covered: (1) decompose_mode is threaded into build_project_model_snapshot (no residual hardcoded fixture); (2) _validate_live_config fails closed without allow_live, explicit live_model, and (for live_diff) a loadable .arena/goal.toml tracked in git HEAD; (3) _select_promotable skips candidates lacking deterministic verification_commands before any live call; (4) code candidates (.py/needs_code_change) are non-promotable unless a configured test command passes (required_missing fail-closed when absent); (5) live patch+provenance are copied to cycle-N/candidate-artifacts before worktree teardown; (6) markdown repair records _current_diff so the recorded patch matches the verified on-disk content, and promotion stages on-disk content not the patch; (7) the report explicitly scopes to bounded one-cycle execution and disclaims broad unattended autonomy. Promotion is doubly guarded (dry_run/allow_promotion gate + staged-set==target + boundary re-check + ff-only merge). Only minor robustness notes remain; none block the bounded run."
}
```
